# Tailwind in CSS modules + loading + icons

## Tailwind-in-CSS-modules
- **Style with Tailwind via `@apply`** inside `.module.css` — prefer `@apply` over `composes: ... from global`; raw CSS only when no utility fits.
- Separator is `_` (e.g. `md_pt-10`, `hover_text-black`).
- **Use arbitrary values when no token fits** (e.g. `@apply py-[13px] w-[100px]`) rather than hand-written CSS.
- Theme extends `@magento/pwa-theme-venia` via `tailwind.config.js` / `theme.js`.
- In a component override, import the **local** `./component.module.css`.
- **Don't assume a stock Tailwind class exists** — the preset has incomplete numeric scales. Confirmed missing: `duration-*`, `size-5` (→ `w-5 h-5`), `min-w-40` (→ `min-w-[10rem]`). When webpack says ``The `X-N` class does not exist``, convert `N` to its rem value and rewrite as `X-[Nrem]` (40 = 10rem), or add it to `theme.js` — don't guess a different numeric step.
- **Never `@apply` a utility inside a class of the same name** (e.g. `.grid { @apply grid }`) — circular dependency, build fails.
- **Responsive by default** — mobile AND desktop; when adjusting one breakpoint, confirm the other still holds.

## Colors — `theme.js` is the single source (hard rule)
- **Grep `theme.js` `extend.colors` before adding** a color.
- **No raw hex anywhere** — `bg-[#hex]`/`text-[#hex]` AND plain CSS `color:`/`background-color:`/`border-color: #hex` are equally forbidden; grep for both before adding.
- **Naming convention by intent:** *semantic group* named after the class/state it backs for shared component-state colors (`field: { DEFAULT, error, disabled }` → `bg-field-error`); *scale-style palette* with sequential numeric suffixes (`gray.1`..`gray.4`, `orange.1`) for general grays/accents — NOT Tailwind's 50–950 scale (collides with `gray-700`/`orange-50`…).
- **Don't duplicate a brand color** into a new palette (keep `primary: '#FF6900'` under `primary`).

## Loading states
- Prefer a **shimmer skeleton that mirrors the real layout** while an API loads (match structure + spacing so layout doesn't jump). Avoid `fullPageLoadingIndicator`.
- Applies to **any async-populated UI** (modals, sections), not just initial load — never render an empty shell while fetching.

## Icons (hard rule)
- New icons in `src/components/Icons/` as JS components with **inline SVG**.
- **Never use `react-feather`** (or other icon libraries) for app icons.
- **From Figma:** when a design node is an SVG icon, clone it into a JS icon component under `src/components/Icons/` — inline the SVG markup. Do not substitute a react-feather equivalent or render the raw asset.
- **Attribute the source** with a one-line comment citing the Figma node (e.g. `// Cloned from Figma \`icon/checked\` (node 115:9791)`).
- **Verify + de-dupe assets** before writing: curl the SVG from the Figma MCP asset server, confirm with `file -b`, and `diff` likely duplicates — byte-identical assets share ONE component.
